      "writtenOn": "2026-07-21T12:21:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"...\" wrapping is Jackson\u0027s JSON string-encoding. It\u0027s gone because the controller returns a String, and Spring\u0027s default @WebMvcTest converters write a String verbatim via StringHttpMessageConverter instead of through Jackson. This is built into @WebMvcTest, not DmiPluginConfig — I confirmed the spec still passes without DmiPluginConfig.",
